      "text": "To find the value(s) of \\( x \\) for which \\( f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\), we need to understand the relationship between a function and its inverse. The inverse function \\( f^{-1} \\) of a function \\( f \\) is defined such that \\( f(f^{-1}(x)) = x \\) and \\( f^{-1}(f(x)) = x \\).\n\nGiven the function \\( f(x) = 3x - 8 \\), we first need to find its inverse \\( f^{-1}(x) \\). To do this, we start by setting \\( y = f(x) \\) and solving for \\( x \\) in terms of \\( y \\):\n\n\\[\ny = 3x - 8\n\\]\n\nAdd 8 to both sides:\n\n\\[\ny + 8 = 3x\n\\]\n\nDivide both sides by 3:\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{y + 8}{3}\n\\]\n\nThus, the inverse function is:\n\n\\[\nf^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x + 8}{3}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the value(s) of \\( x \\) for which \\( f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\). This means we need to solve the equation:\n\n\\[\n3x - 8 = \\frac{x + 8}{3}\n\\]\n\nTo eliminate the fraction, multiply both sides by 3:\n\n\\[\n3(3x - 8) = x + 8\n\\]\n\nDistribute the 3 on the left side:\n\n\\[\n9x - 24 = x + 8\n\\]\n\nSubtract \\( x \\) from both sides:\n\n\\[\n8x - 24 = 8\n\\]\n\nAdd 24 to both sides:\n\n\\[\n8x = 32\n\\]\n\nDivide both sides by 8:\n\n\\[\nx = 4\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we substitute \\( x = 4 \\) back into the original function \\( f(x) \\) and its inverse \\( f^{-1}(x) \\):\n\n\\[\nf(4) = 3(4) - 8 = 12 - 8 = 4\n\\]\n\n\\[\nf^{-1}(4) = \\frac{4 + 8}{3} = \\frac{12}{3} = 4\n\\]\n\nSince both sides are equal, our solution is verified. Therefore, the value of \\( x \\) for which \\( f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{4}\n\\]",
